### 3.1 Authentication & User Profiles (P0) — Partly built
- **Built:** sign up and sign in with email and password; email confirmation required before writing reviews or enquiries. Roles: parent, school_admin (a school's staff), admin (Kidscover); users cannot change their own role.
- **Planned:** Google, Microsoft and phone (OTP) sign-in; profile picture or stock avatar; settings (dark mode, push notifications, biometric login, language).

### 3.2 Location-Based Discovery (P0) — Built
- **Use my location:** the phone's position (rounded to about 100 m) is used only to measure distance; it is never stored in the database or on the phone. Refusing permission leaves everything else working.
- **Distance on every school, "Nearest first", "Within 2 / 5 / 10 km"** (straight-line, labelled as such). Schools without coordinates are left out of near-me lists only.
- **Drive time by car** (Google Routes API, traffic-aware): "Weekday 7:30 am" (the next school-run departure, India time) or "Right now", for the schools on screen, 20 at a time. Google plans car trips by departure time only, so "arrive by" is shown as a departure at school-run time.
- **Cost control:** limits in the database, changeable by an admin: 20 lookups per parent per day and 500 schools per day for the whole app by default. Kidscover stores only a count of lookups per parent per day, never where anyone was.
- **Planned:** location fallback order (GPS > address book > last session > ask); dashboard tiles (schools in area, admissions open / closed); arrival time computed from each school's own start time.

### 3.3 Discover List, Categories & Filters (P0) — Built
- **Categories:** every place is a *school* (preschool to class 12, junior colleges included), an *after-school class* (music, dance, sports, art, abacus, tuition) or a *college* (degree, engineering, business, law, medicine, teacher training). The app opens on Schools; the other two are one tap away. Places not for children (driving schools, gyms, IELTS classes, shops, offices) are hidden.
- **Search** by name or area; **filters:** level (preschool, primary, secondary, not stated), daycare, board (with "also show schools whose board is not known yet"), Google rating (with "include unrated"), sort (A to Z, best rated, nearest). Level, daycare and board apply to schools only and are set aside, not cleared, on the other lists.
- **Planned:** True Total Cost of Ownership filter (tuition, transport, cafeteria, uniform, admission and registration fees in one annual figure); established age of the institution.

### 3.4 School Detail Page (P1) — Built
- **Photo:** uploaded by the school (it confirms it may publish it) or a free-licensed Wikimedia Commons photo shown with its author and licence; with no photo, a drawn school in colours of its own. No paid or copyrighted image sources.
- **Facts, each with its source:** levels (from the name, Google and, once accepted, the school's website); board ("confirmed by CBSE's own record", "from the school's website", "from the school's name"); admission status with year ("from the school's website, checked Sep 2026"); Google rating; parent reviews.
- **Facilities** (20 kinds: cafeteria, open and indoor play, pool, courts, library, science / computer / maths / STEM / AI labs, smart classrooms, auditorium, art and music rooms, school bus, medical room, CCTV, air conditioning, special needs support, teacher-student ratio).
- **Achievements** the school claims: class 10 and class 12 results, college placements, notable alumni, awards; newest first; each marked with its source and linked to where it was published.
- **Ask about admissions** (schools only) and the school's website link.
- **Planned:** enrolment size; fee breakdown (TCO); side-by-side comparison of up to 4 schools.

### 3.5 Admissions Enquiries (P1) — Built
- A short form (which class, roughly when, the question). It deliberately does **not** ask for a child's name or date of birth.
- A conversation per school under **Enquiries**, with an unread count. Replies show as coming from "the school". One open enquiry per school; at most 10 new enquiries a day; a confirmed email is required; either side can close, writing again reopens.
- **Partner Portal inbox** for answering, with "need a reply" counts.
- **Planned:** partner schools' own staff answer their enquiries; the Kidscover Standard admission form pushed to a partner school's CRM by webhook; outbound-click logging for non-partner schools; push notifications for replies.

### 3.6 Parent Reviews & Moderation (P1) — Built
- Anonymous reviews (rating, optional title, text, relationship to the school), one per parent per school; a new or edited review is pending until a moderator publishes it; parents can report others' reviews; the Parent Reviews tab in the portal publishes, rejects and handles reports.

### 3.7 School Data Pipeline — Built
- **Import:** Google Places (Mumbai / Thane box) for names, addresses, coordinates, types and ratings.
- **Quality rules and categories** in the database (from the name first, Google's type second); an admin can move any single place or hide it, with a reason shown for every automatic decision.
- **Website reader** (edge function, run by an admin in batches): obeys robots.txt, identifies itself, reads the home page and up to three more pages per school, refuses private addresses and re-checks redirects. It finds:
  - **Board:** English, Marathi and Hindi wording, and CBSE affiliation numbers checked against CBSE's public record (confirmed only when the record is in Maharashtra and matches the PIN, website or name).
  - **Levels:** ranges such as "Nursery to Grade 10", "Classes I to X" and "iyatta 5 vi te 10 vi", plus named sections.
  - **Admission status** with its year; old notices are marked and cannot be used.
  - **Facilities**, including a teacher-student ratio.
  - **Claimed achievements.**

  On a website shared by several schools, only this school's pages are read.
- **Review:** everything found waits in the School Data tab with the sentence and page it came from; nothing reaches parents until an admin accepts it; what the school or Kidscover entered is never overwritten by a website finding. Schools are re-read every 30 days.
- **Not used (and not worked around):** the CISCE directory (behind a CAPTCHA), open UDISE+ extracts (no board column, no licence), and parts of CBSE's site that refuse automated access.

### 3.8 School Profiles, School Staff & the Change Log — Built
- A Kidscover admin adds a school's staff by email (they sign up first); staff can edit only their own school: photo, facilities, achievements.
- Changes go live at once. Database triggers record every change (who, their role, when, before and after), so nothing escapes the log. A Kidscover admin sees all changes, and can undo the latest change to anything; the undo is logged too.
- Photos upload to a public storage bucket, one folder per school, JPEG / PNG / WebP up to 5 MB; only that school's staff (or an admin) can write to its folder.

### 3.9 Look and Feel — Built
- A warm palette (violet, coral, sunshine and mint on lavender), a logo, a welcome drawing of a parent walking a child to school on the sign-in screen, a welcome banner that changes with the list, a picture on every school card, and icons for categories, facilities and achievements. All drawings are made in code, so there is nothing to license.

### 3.10 Partner Portal (Admin Web App) — Built
- **Tabs:**
  - Admissions Pipeline;
  - Admissions Enquiries (inbox);
  - Parent Reviews (moderation);
  - School Data (website reader and review);
  - Categories;
  - School Profiles (edit any school, staff, change log with undo).
- **Panels:** data pipeline sweep, and drive-time usage and limits with a live test button.
- School staff get their own dashboard showing only their school.

